        "Khushu' is inner humility, stillness of the limbs, and attentive contemplation of what one is reciting.\n\nPractical Anchors for Khushu':\n- Prepare before the Takbir: Perform wudu mindfully, arrive before iqamah, and eliminate immediate physical distractions.\n- Contemplate the Words: Recite slowly (Tartil). When saying 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen', remember Allah responds directly: 'My servant has praised Me' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Fix the Gaze: Direct your gaze respectfully at the place of prostration (Sujud), rather than looking around.\n- Remember the Final Prayer: The Prophet (peace be upon him) advised: 'Pray as if it were your farewell prayer' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171)." to "Khushu' dil ki aajizi, aaza ka sukoon, aur jo padh rahe hain us par dhyan se ghaur karna hai.\n\nKhushu' ke amli tareeqe:\n- Takbeer se pehle tayyari: Dhyan se wuzu karein, iqamah se pehle pahunchein, aur saamne ki jismani rukawatein door karein.\n- Alfaaz par ghaur karein: Aahista (Tarteel se) padhein. Jab 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen' kahein to yaad rakhein ke Allah seedha jawab deta hai: 'Mere bande ne meri tareef ki' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Nazar jama kar rakhein: Idhar udhar dekhne ke bajaye adab se sajde ki jagah (Sujud) par nazar rakhein.\n- Aakhri namaz yaad rakhein: Nabi (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ne nasihat farmayi: 'Aise namaz padho jaise yeh tumhari alvida namaz ho' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171).",
